[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! Hyperlinks (OSC 8, `references/modern/osc8_hyperlinks.md`): the links a                                             [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! grid's cells point to, each held once, and the cells' links, held per row                                           [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! beside the cells for the rows that have any.                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//!                                                                                                                     [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! A cell's link is a `u16` in its row's array, 0 for none and otherwise one                                           [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! more than the link's place in the table. Only a cell with contents has                                              [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! one: an erased cell keeps whatever number it had, unread, until a glyph                                             [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! is printed there, which always writes its link; so erasing, which blanks                                            [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! cells, never touches the arrays. The second half of a wide glyph has its                                            [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! first half's link.                                                                                                  [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//!                                                                                                                     [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! The table counts the numbers in the arrays (an erased cell's too), so the                                           [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! links no row has are found without reading the rows: every change to an                                             [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m//! array holds and releases the numbers it writes and drops.                                                           [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0muse std::collections::HashMap;                                                                                          [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0muse std::sync::Arc;                                                                                                     [39;49m
